## Register Analysis

Key registers at crash:
- RSI (chanctx_conf): 0x0000000000000000  <-- NULL pointer being dereferenced
- RDI: 0x0000000000000000
- CR2 (fault address): 0x0000000000000000
- R13: 0x0000000000000000

The crash instruction "48 8b 0e" is "mov rcx, [rsi]" - dereferencing NULL RSI.

## Modules at Crash Time

mt7925e mt7925_common mt792x_lib mt76_connac_lib mt76 mac80211 cfg80211

## Suggested Fix

In mt7925_vif_connect_iter(), add NULL check for vif->bss_conf.chanctx_conf
before proceeding with the add_dev call. Interfaces that have been disconnected
during the reset window should be skipped.

Example:
  if (!vif->bss_conf.chanctx_conf)
      return;

## Reproduction

1. Connect to WiFi 7 AP with MLO enabled
2. Roam between APs or trigger disconnect/reconnect
3. If association is rejected/times out during MCU message timeouts, reset work triggers crash

## Related Issues

This is the THIRD occurrence of this bug today:
- crash-2026-01-10-reset-work-null-ptr.log (18:39:17) - first occurrence
- crash-2026-01-10-2112-reset-work-null-vif.log (21:12:53) - second occurrence
- crash-2026-01-10-2123-reset-work-null-vif.log (21:23:03) - this crash

All occur during reset recovery when vif state has changed (disconnected/disassociated)
between timeout detection and reset work execution. The race window is between the
association timeout and the reset work handler iterating interfaces.

## Frequency

Three crashes in approximately 3 hours of use, all triggered by AP roaming.
This is a critical reliability issue for mobile/roaming use cases.
